{"name":"Safflower Scarlet","hex":"#e83929","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated thistle-like plant, Carthamus tinctorius, family Asteraceae, now grown mainly for its oil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safflower"},{"term":"scarlet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brilliant red colour sometimes tinged with orange.","Cloth of a scarlet color."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright red colour.","Sinful or whorish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarlet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safflower","blocks":[{"text":"Safflower, also false saffron, is a highly branched, herbaceous, thistle-like annual plant in the family Asteraceae. It is one of the world's oldest crops; today, it is commercially cultivated for vegetable oil extracted from the seeds. Plants are 30 to 150 cm tall with globular flower heads having yellow, orange, or red flowers. Each branch will usually have from one to five flower heads containing 15 to 20 seeds per head. Safflower is native to arid environments having seasonal rain. It grows a deep taproot which enables it to thrive in such environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Safflower.jpg/330px-Safflower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safflower","wikidata":"Q156625"},{"title":"Scarlet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet is a bright red color, sometimes with a slightly orange tinge. In the spectrum of visible light, and on the traditional color wheel, it is one-quarter of the way between red and orange, slightly less orange than vermilion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/RCMP-female-officer.jpg/330px-RCMP-female-officer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(color)","wikidata